<bx:script>
import bxModules.bxai.models.mcp.MCPRequestProcessor;

// Rexor's own MCP server (registered in Application.bx) - exposes the
// platform's actions (list_target_types, create_test_plan, run_probes) as
// MCP tools, same transport bx-ai's own client expects. Reached here as
// /api/mcp.bxm?server=rexor, both by the chat agent (loopback, server-side)
// and by any external MCP client that wants to drive Rexor directly.
//
// NOTE: the hosted bx-ai docs show `MCPRequestProcessor::startHttp()`, but
// that method doesn't exist on the real 3.5.0 class (verified against the
// real error: "The key [startHttp] was not found... Valid keys are
// [..., processHttp, ...]") - `processHttp()` is the real one.
MCPRequestProcessor::processHttp();
</bx:script>
